  "honest_limits": [
    "The E. coli calibration uses THIS repo's 600-window samples, not P2's exact fit windows, so it validates the implementation rather than reproducing their measurement identically.",
    "The spec names the degenerate VALUE but not the WIDTH it was observed at, and this corpus reaches that value at k=14 rather than k=12. Which width P2 used is unresolved and is the one thing that would change how the two curves line up.",
    "Zero exact duplicate elements in either cell, so density is not inflated by repeated sequences -- but near-duplicates (mutational series of a shared parent) were NOT measured, and they would raise the ratio without adding diversity.",
    "Single strand as given. Pooling both strands would raise the ratio and is not done here.",
    "This is a property of the generator's training folds only. Folds 9 and 10 were not read.",
    "A count-model occupancy statistic says nothing about what a NEURAL model could extract from the same corpus; it bounds the count-model class the question was posed about.",
    "The calibration gap is CLOSED: it was neither definitional nor a corpus difference but STRIDE. Under P2's actual non-overlapping convention this implementation reproduces 1.002 within the statistic's own across-sample spread."
  ],
  "CALIBRATION_POINT_CLOSED": {
    "date": "2026-11-22",
    "P2s_answer": "the 1.002 figure is neither k=12 nor k=14 of this arm's primary. It is a UNIT-EMISSION table whose cell is a (6 bp context, 6-MER symbol) pair over a space of 4^6 x 4^6 = 4^12, which is why it superficially reads as a 12 bp figure. Each of its observations consumes six bases of output rather than one. P2 names this its own defect: it demanded reproducibility and then gave a value without its parameterisation.",
    "I_THEN_COMPUTED_THEIR_STATISTIC_AND_IT_COINCIDES_WITH_MY_k12": {
      "the_observation": "a (6-mer context, 6-mer symbol) PAIR *is* a 12-mer, and so is a 12-mer context. Under a stride-1 convention the two statistics therefore count the SAME distinct 12-mers, and P2's redirection away from the context-wise primary is numerically a no-op.",
