      "the_N_obs_delta_is_exactly_one_position_per_sequence": "58,998 for K562 and 36,876 for HepG2, equal to the element counts, because the unit-emission span needs L-11 start positions while a next-base context needs L-12. That boundary convention is the entire difference.",
      "so_the_semantics_differ_and_the_COUNT_does_not": "what a cell MEANS differs -- a unit emission versus a next-base conditional -- and that distinction is real and worth keeping. But the two reduce to the same occupancy count, so the original k=12 figure was already the right comparison."
    },
    "WHICH_MEANS_THE_NUMERICAL_GAP_IS_NOT_DEFINITIONAL_AND_IS_STILL_OPEN": {
      "my_ecoli_on_THEIR_statistic": {
        "min": 1.0115,
        "max": 1.0264,
        "mean": 1.0156,
